          "text": "## Branch XI — post-war recombination\n\nThe defeat of Nazi Germany is a major historical rupture, but the institutional and technical fields crossing the war do not all terminate with the regime. Race science and eugenics were transnational before the war. Nazi lawyers studied United States racial law while formulating parts of the Nuremberg legal regime. Operation Paperclip moved German scientists and technicians, including Nazi-affiliated personnel, into United States programmes. The Gehlen organisation was established under US Army intelligence and later connected to the CIA while drawing heavily on former German intelligence personnel. Denazification was incomplete and many professionals/officials returned to positions in post-war institutions.\n\nThe working theorem is therefore:\n\n> **Defeat of one explicit ideological configuration did not dissolve the administrative, scientific, racial, financial, intelligence, technological and imperial forms out of which it emerged; these were selectively repudiated, transformed, preserved and recombined.**\n\nThis is an evidence programme, not one undifferentiated continuity claim. Each conduit must be followed institution by institution, person by person, technique by technique and concept by concept.\n"
