          "text": "The image gathers two recoveries. The first belongs to the word technē, in the genealogy Heidegger recovered: technē \"linked with the word epistēmē,\" both \"names for knowing in the widest sense\"; technē belonging \"to bringing-forth, to poiēsis\"; \"it is as revealing, and not as manufacturing, that technē is a bringing-forth\" (*QCT*, pp. 12–13). The definition of poiēsis he quotes is Diotima's, from *Symposium* 205b — \"every occasion for whatever passes over and goes forward into presencing from that which is not presencing is poiēsis\" — and the same banquet gives the essay its symbolon in Aristophanes' speech: emission and return seated at one table from the beginning (the connection is the essay's own, **Argued**). An attunement instrument is technē in this recovered sense — a made thing whose making reveals, coordinating cycles it does not own for an observer it does not replace — which is the mechanism's exact difference from the net of §2 · #3: both are consummate craft; one renders cycles mutually readable for a situated observer, the other renders persons capturable for a convened audience."
